.TH SRV-TUNE 1 "2026-10-17" "srv-tune 0.3.0" "System administration"
.SH NAME
srv-tune \- Linux server optimizer: SCAN, RECOMMEND, APPLY, VERIFY, ROLLBACK-IF-BROKEN
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B srv-tune scan
.RB [ \-\-json
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-diff
.IR BASELINE.json ]
.RB [ \-\-lang
.IR fa | en ]
.br
.B srv-tune recommend
.RB [ \-\-lang
.IR fa | en ]
.br
.B srv-tune apply \-\-profile
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-only
.IR mod [,mod]]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-with\-ssh ]
.RB [ \-\-with\-firewall ]
.RB [ \-\-with\-registry ]
.RB [ \-\-with\-dot ]
.RB [ \-\-mirror
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-dns\-extra
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B srv-tune rollback
.RI [ id ]
|
.B list-backups
|
.B status
|
.BI explain " module"
.br
.B srv-tune benchmark
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR DIR ]
|
.BR \-\-compare
.IR BEFORE " " AFTER
.br
.B srv-tune audit
|
.B update
|
.B uninstall
|
.BI confirm " guard-id"
.br
.B srv-tune health
.RB [ \-\-json
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B srv-tune repair
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-json
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
srv-tune tunes a Linux server in five auditable stages: read-only
.BR scan ,
profile
.BR recommend ,
.BR apply ,
.BR verify ,
and automatic rollback when a health check fails.
Every changed file is backed up first; writes are atomic temp-to-move
drop-ins; re-runs are idempotent.
.PP
Core modules (stable): limits, network, kernel, dns, mirror (apt).
Registry mirrors (pip_mirror, npm_mirror, docker_mirror) are tool-gated
and need
.BR \-\-with\-registry .
ssh, firewall and fail2ban are EXPERIMENTAL: they need an explicit flag
plus a typed confirmation, guarded by a timed auto-revert.
.PP
Registry mirrors are NOT signed like apt. DNS tier-optional resolvers see
every query. Nothing from
.I data/
is used until a human verifies it (see DATA-REVIEW in the source tree).
.PP
.B health
is read-only: it replays the post-apply checks of every module recorded in
the applied-changes log, reports unconfirmed guards whose timed
auto-revert is still pending, and exits 1 on any failed check. Run it as
root for full coverage (module checks are skipped otherwise). It performs
no writes itself; the mirror check may refresh apt metadata.
.PP
.B repair
first replays the same post-apply checks, then re-applies only the drifted
modules, using the profile recorded at apply time, with the apply rails:
fresh backup, verify, automatic rollback on failure. Requires root.
Modules still gated by an opt-in flag (see
.BR \-\-with\-ssh ,
.BR \-\-with\-firewall ,
.BR \-\-with\-registry )
are reported, never silently applied. With
.B \-\-dry\-run
it prints the exact diffs and writes nothing. Exit: 0 clean or repaired; 1
nothing repairable or the apply failed; 2 usage, root, or missing profile
record (log lines from before profile recording are refused).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " " \fINAME\fR
generic, web, database, docker, vpn-tunnel, low-ram, or custom (with
.BR \-\-config ).
Without
.B \-\-profile
the scanner recommendation is offered on one Enter.
.TP
.BR \-\-only " " \fImod\fR[,\fImod\fR]
Apply only the named modules.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show the exact diff plus the reason for every setting. Changes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Non-interactive: accept prompts and skip typed confirmations. The
.BR \-\-with\-*
opt-in flags are still required.
.TP
.B \-\-with\-ssh
Enlist the ssh module (typed SSH-YES still required without
.BR \-\-yes ).
.TP
.B \-\-with\-firewall
Enlist firewall/fail2ban (typed FIREWALL-YES still required without
.BR \-\-yes ).
.TP
.B \-\-with\-registry
Enlist pip/npm/docker registry mirrors (typed REGISTRY-YES still
required without
.BR \-\-yes ).
.TP
.B \-\-with\-dot
Enlist DNS-over-TLS: applied only on the systemd-resolved backend and
only when TCP port 853 is reachable on both winning resolvers (checked
live; refused otherwise). Off by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-mirror " " \fIURL\fR
Use this registry URL instead of the curated pick (https only). Also the
way back to an official origin, which is never auto-selected.
.TP
.BR \-\-dns\-extra " " \fINAME\fR
Add a tier-optional resolver by ID (repeatable, comma-separated). Prints
the third-party disclosure and needs typed DNS-EXTRA-YES without
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.BR \-\-lang " " \fIfa|en\fR
UI language (default en).
.TP
.BR \-\-json " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the scan report as JSON (scan), the health check report (health),
or the pre-repair health report (repair).
.TP
.BR \-\-diff " " \fIBASELINE.json\fR
Compare the fresh scan against a scan JSON saved earlier with
.BR \-\-json :
print only the changed, added and removed keys plus the score and
profile change. Reporting only; exits 0 unless the baseline is missing
or is not a flat scan JSON (then 2).
.SH SAFETY
Always run
.B \-\-dry\-run
first. Keep one proven session open for anything touching ssh/firewall
and confirm from a NEW session. Registry and DNS-extra changes print
their risks and need typed phrases. No telemetry, no hidden network calls.
.SH FILES
.I profiles/*.conf
\- shipped profiles (registry modules are never listed there).
.br
.I data/*.list
\- curated mirrors/resolvers with owner, docs, tier and verified fields.
.br
.I /var/lib/srv-tune/backups/<id>/
\- per-apply backups restored by
.BR rollback .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (or clean skip), 1 on module failure with rollback, 2 on
usage/preflight errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ufw (8),
.BR nft (8)
.PP
Source tree docs: README.md, README.fa.md, docs/TESTING-VM.md,
docs/DATA-REVIEW.md.
